# Fantasy / Tools UI

Read `docs/PRODUCT.md` first. User-facing name is **Fantasy**, not Draft Hub.

## Layout

- Resolve the screen in `frontend/src/livingSurfaces.js` and open that `page` / `copy` before changing chrome.
- Pages: `HubPage` with `hub-experience-page` when the surface is a decision page.
- Hero + sticky summary: `HubExperienceHero`, `HubExperienceLayout`, `HubExperienceSummary` in `HubUILayout.jsx`.
- Sections: `HubSection`, `HubTableCard`, `HubToolbar`, `HubAlert` / `HubAlertStack`.
- Intro copy: `HubTabIntro` only when the page is not already using the experience hero.
- Live draft (`DraftRoom` while a draft is running): keep the board-first layout. Do not add the two-column settings chrome.
- Do not create a second hero, chip, or summary component. Extend the existing ones.
- On phone, Fantasy destinations use the header picker (`HubSubnav` sheet), not the destination scroller. A one-row league strip (name + caret) sits under the picker; New league / Sync league live in that caret. Needs attention is one line on the strip. Account lives in More.
- Idle Draft, Mock, and the live room share `DraftSeat`. Do not fork YOU / Open · Take tiles.

## Copy and data

- User-visible strings belong in `*Presentation.js` (`rulesPresentation.js`, `leagueHomePresentation.js`, `gameCenterPresentation.js`, `dfsToolPresentation.js`, `bestBallPresentation.js`, `insightsPresentation.js`, `leagueAccessCopy.js`, `vibeRankingsPresentation.js`, `strategyRankPresentation.js`, `capPlannerPresentation.js`, `officeContractsPresentation.js`). Home and Game center share `interpretStandings`. Do not invent a 1–10 seed from 0–0.
- Page copy states the decision and the cost of getting it wrong. No slogan that could sit on another app.
- Rules preview, validation, and summary: `mergeLeagueRules`, `validateLeagueSettings`, `contractSchedule`, `rulesSummary`.
- Rules templates confirm and fill the form. They do not save. Draft behavior is an open section. Save stays off until the form is dirty and valid.
- At a glance on Rules is “Currently saved” or “Preview of your changes”. Hero chips are status, not the page primary.
- Free-agent button/banner copy: `acquisitionWindow.js`.
- Free agents rows always show Bid or Add. When locked, disable with Adds open after the draft — do not omit the action. Hide Vs cost until contracts exist. Fold tier into the player cell. Desktop virtualizes against page scroll; do not nest a table scroller. How adds work lives in the acquisition banner.
- Home next-action voice: `leagueHomePresentation.js`.

## Chat

- Use `FantasyChatDock` on shared Fantasy pages when a real league is selected.
- Keep it a flush edge launcher you can drag to a new edge. Horizontal type only — do not rotate the chip. Hide is not the only placement control. On phone, default to the bottom-right above the tab bar with a safe-area inset. The dismiss control sits on the bubble, never off the right edge.
- Opening is a side drawer. Closing returns to the launcher.
- House the full thread on Home as a locker rail. Do not show the edge launcher on Home. Do not add a Chat tab or destination.
- Hide for solo / unconnected contexts.
- Hide in a live draft room that already has integrated chat.
- Do not add a Chat tab under Roster management.

## League behavior

- Rules are readable by members (`Commissioner managed`). Roster management is commissioner/co-commissioner only.
- Old `/hub/office` and commissioner routes must keep working; redirect, do not break bookmarks.
- Players-tab adds follow the calendar. Offseason trades: surviving contracts only.
- Draft availability shows current and future times only. Commissioners lock a promising overlap as draft night from the shared calendar.
- Idle Draft is one featured job: the shared calendar plus a compact room strip. While the calendar is open, the date/time form, invite essays, and a second Who is in list stay collapsed. When the calendar is closed and no night is locked, the date/time form is the card primary and Start live draft is secondary.
- Suggested bid, wherever it renders (Strategy, Free agents, live room), shows the league scoring name and the Rules risk posture beside the number.
- Freshness is one shared `ensureLeagueFreshness` call. Do not add a second `/freshness` fetch on a destination.
- Cache `/api/hub/home` like other destinations so a tab switch is not a 6s refetch.
- Do not fetch Projections APIs (`/api/injuries`, `meta/*`, `ros/*`, `predict/*`, `draft/*`) on Fantasy pages that do not render them.
- Headshots must match roster photos (`HubMediaImg` / existing media helpers). Request the painted size (`?w=48|96|256` for hub media; ESPN combiner / Sleeper thumb for remotes). Do not fetch the studio original for a 22px mark.
- `GET /api/hub/value-sheet` is one in-flight request per season/rules key. Cap-sheet updates must not abort and refetch it.
- Chat polls back off when the tab is hidden. Do not keep a 12s `chat/league/messages` loop on a background tab.
- Strategy face-off pairs the same position only. Do not pair RB vs WR as a FLEX toss-up.

## Visual

- Tokens from `tokens.css`, `product-hierarchy.css`, `product-rhythm.css`, and `fantasy-phone.css`. No one-off neon, no new accent color.
- On phone, filter / tab / sort bars use `.hub-page-sticky` (the Insights strip). Experience summary labels stack above their values.
- Ten managers is a picker (`HubFilterMenu`), not a swipe strip.
- Rosters defaults to the league-wide Overpay/Bargain list. Expire chips are status (Extendable), never a question.
- Every Fantasy, Tools, and Projections surface uses token padding and even gutters on mobile and desktop. Do not pack labels flush to a border or rule, or drop type below `--text-xs`.
- Laptop: summary rail may drop under the hero. No horizontal page scroll at 1024 / 1280 / 1440.
- Player boards (Free agents, Best ball) use labeled Pos / Sort menus. Do not mix filter and sort in one unlabeled chip row.
- Long Tools tables window against page scroll. Do not nest a `.table-wrap` scroller.
- Primary save/action stays visible. Disabled controls explain why.
- Roster management pane switcher is the four pills only. Do not inline group labels with the chips.
- Contracts writes go through the pending-changes tray. Drop is not a one-click delete.
- Numbered step sequences include every visible step or drop the numerals.
- Do not keep hidden Fantasy panes in the DOM of another destination. Unmount keep-alives when the tab is not showing.
- Rank bars share a fixed track and a field scale (near the minimum, or delta from first). Never let the value label steal track width. Do not paint every bar teal/green.
- Insights Overview keeps the tab strip live and skeletons the three cards. Do not cover Insights with a think scrim.
- Trades Send / Get / Cut expose `aria-pressed` and an accessible name that includes the player and destination. Auto-check the package; do not leave Propose unlocked on an unchecked deal.
- Fantasy forms use HubFilterMenu, not native `<select>`.
- Cap leftover after a move sits next to the cut and bid controls. Every leftover, against-cap, and roster figure names what it counts.
